 <title>The Yaf_Application class</title>
 <titleabbrev>Yaf_Application</titleabbrev>

 <partintro>

<!-- {{{ Yaf_Application intro -->
  <section xml:id="yaf-application.intro">
   &reftitle.intro;
   <simpara>
    <classname>Yaf_Application</classname> provides a bootstrapping facility
    for applications which provides reusable resources, common- and
    module-based bootstrap classes and dependency checking.
   </simpara>
   <note>
    <simpara>
     <classname>Yaf_Application</classname> implements the singleton
     pattern, and <classname>Yaf_Application</classname> can not be
     serialized or unserialized, which will cause problems when you try
     to use PHPUnit to write some test cases for Yaf.
    </simpara>
    <simpara>
     You may use the <literal>@backupGlobals</literal> annotation of
     PHPUnit to control the backup and restore operations for global
     variables, thus solving this problem.
    </simpara>
   </note>
  </section>
<!-- }}} -->

